{
 "status": "measured",
 "method": "Navigation memory on the GPU: parity with the engine and cost per agent.\n\nOne command from the Mac stages everything on dev-ubuntu, runs one gq job and\ncollects the report::\n\n    python3 scripts/navsim/gpumem/bench.py remote --agents 64,256,1024,2048\n\nThe gq VRAM request and the allocator cap follow the largest N (about 1.8 MiB\nper agent with the readout batch), so larger N needs only another list, for\nexample ``--agents 4096,8192`` with the services stopped (``--skip-parity``\nsaves the parity minute). Each run appends to ``runs`` in the report; parity\nis kept from the last run that had it.\n\nCommands inside the job:\n  parity  every readout of every capture through the engine (navsim_memory_ref,\n          ctypes, built from this checkout) and the batched port, bit for bit;\n          the HD net's argmax actions on both inputs, each with its own GRU state\n  scale   per-agent update/readout cost and VRAM for a list of N, one process\n          per N; captures repeat across agents with shifted starts",
 "implementation": {
  "choice": "CUDA C++ through a PyTorch extension (torch.utils.cpp_extension.load), not Warp",
  "reasons": [
   "Bitwise parity needs explicit compiler control: nvcc --fmad=false, IEEE division/sqrt, no fast math; the same header also builds for the CPU (one lane) to check logic against the engine without a GPU.",
   "Order-preserving ingestion is warp-synchronous: one warp per agent and grid, rays in slot order with __syncwarp between rays, the 32 lanes splitting one ray's distinct DDA cells; this relies on __syncwarp/__ballot_sync, which Warp kernels do not expose.",
   "The readout writes torch CUDA tensors in place (CHW float32), the HD net's input batch."
  ],
  "kernels": {
   "prepare": "warp per agent: pose, reset, path history, fresh slots (ballot compaction), water list",
   "ingest": "warp per agent and grid: centring, familiar window, ordered ray DDA, water patches",
   "read": "thread per output cell: gathers the <=3x3 world cells mapping into it in world order, classifies, merges by the engine's precedence, quantises, writes 10 planes"
  },
  "source": "scripts/navsim/gpumem/memory_kernels.h"
 },
 "warp": "not used (CUDA C++ extension, see implementation)",
